[2m─── pymtg/utils/retry.py:0-0 ───[0m
[94m[bug · low][0m wait() uses `self.attempt - 1` as the backoff attempt index. In the documented usage,
record_failure() increments attempt to 1 on the first failure, so wait() computes backoff with
attempt=0 — correct. BUT if a user calls wait() before record_failure() (attempt still 0), this
computes calculate_backoff(attempt=-1), yielding backoff_factor * (2**-1) = backoff_factor/2, a
small but unintended value. There is no guard preventing this misuse, and the method name 'wait'
doesn't signal that record_failure must be called first. Consider computing the attempt index from
self.attempt directly (since after increment it equals the number of failures so far, and the next
