[93m[test · medium][0m The 429 retry-after test uses `mock_response.headers.get.return_value = "10"`.
Because `headers` is a MagicMock, this configures `.get()` to return "10" for ANY key. The test
therefore cannot detect whether the provider reads the correct `Retry-After` header name — it would
pass even if the implementation looked up a wrong header key. Consider using a real dict
(`mock_response.headers = {"Retry-After": "10"}`) or configure `side_effect` keyed on the specific
header name so a wrong lookup would return a different value (or None), e.g.:

```python
mock_response.headers.get.side_effect = lambda key, default=None: "10" if key == "Retry-After" else
default
```
This way, if the provider reads the wrong header key, the test would fail because `retry_after`
would not be 10.

